Evaluation scripts (data/scripts/eval)
======================================

These scripts turn the raw run logs in data/raw_data/ into the LaTeX table /
figure fragments under figs/ (ALL_T1020: with BORA_FIG_DRY=1, a dry run's
data/raw_data/dry/ into figs/dry/; a missing log prints a visible
"missing" box or omits a pending same-sample row). They share helpers from ../common.py, including
SERVER_TO_USE, which selects the data-collection server (gcpm1 / jet1tb) for
all server-specific logs. Run each from this folder (python3 <name>.py); each
prints the path it wrote.


RUNALL.sh
---------
Driver: runs every generator below, then check_data_server.py last. A failing
generator (e.g. a dataset whose real dump is still regenerating) is reported
but does not stop the run; the exit code is the number of failed generators.
Usage: bash RUNALL.sh


Python files
------------
datasets.py           Table 1 (tab:datasets): the Mal/Dna/Dlp dataset rows --
                      corpus size, document count, and regex-set size, measured
                      live from the source corpora and rule sets.

effectiveness.py      Tables 2/5/6 (§6.3 + App. C.2): the approximation-
                      effectiveness tables (pair-level + by-file-size), from
                      the tier-discharge dump any_server/eval_effective.txt.

gen_lkup_info.py      Table 7 (tbl:lkup, App. C.3): lookup-table composition
                      -- the five lookup categories x three datasets, from
                      any_server/lookup_stats.dat.

gen_component_cost.py Table 8 (tbl:component-cost, App. C.3): per-circuit cost
                      profile (R1CS per input byte, split across CP/SDE/DFA/
                      framework tiers). Needs a COST-instrumented dump; a dataset without
                      one yet gets a single "***" placeholder row.

gen_overall_perf.py   Table 3 (tbl:overall-perf, §6.5): stage-level performance
                      breakdown (select / commit / fold and compression parts)
                      per dataset.

gen_scale_all.py      Figure 8 (fig:scale-regex, App. C.3): regex-set
                      scalability figure -- per-step circuit size and proof
                      time vs the fraction of the regex set, from the
                      any_server scale bundle (scale_data_gdb.tgz).

dna_reef_bora.py      Table 9 (tab:dna-reef-bora, App. C.4): Reef per-bucket
                      cost vs BORA on chr17 x NCBI, with the Reef-log parser
                      reused by the comparison generators.

gen_zombie_table.py   Table 10 (tab:zombie-data, App. D.4): Zombie per arm L_T
                      (1/2/4 KB): R1CS and proof size from the sweep log,
                      prove/verify time from the same-sample TSV (D5).

gen_compare_measured.py
                      Sec. 6.5 measured comparison (tab:compare-measured, W203):
                      Reef 60 sampled rules vs BORA all rules on Dna, Zombie
                      vs BORA on the same e-mails per arm on Dlp. Replaces
                      gen_compare_all.py (old Table 4, deleted).

count_loc.py          Implementation/eval: counts author-owned Rust lines in
                      new_zkregplus by module (vendored/upstream code excluded).

extract_acc_state_rate.py
                      Off-path analysis tool, not run by RUNALL.sh: the
                      AC-DFA accepting-state density rho behind the "sparse
                      match locations" remark (Complexity, App. B.2.5).  It
                      writes no LaTeX fragment -- it prints a per-dataset
                      summary.  Its input, any_server/dump_acc_state_ratio.txt,
                      is not shipped; regenerate it first (see the recipe in
                      the script docstring and zkp_driver.rs:8748-8753).

check_data_server.py  Data-provenance check (run last by RUNALL.sh): verifies
                      every file under raw_data/{gcpm1,jet1tb} was collected on
                      the matching server (config-dump RAM is authoritative),
                      and that each *.tgz member's self-reported task matches the
                      archive name. Reports violations / unknowns / task
                      mismatches; does not write to figs/.
